WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.734
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.534
you know from his work
in "Lovecraft Country,"

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.834
"The Harder They Fall,"

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.167
and Marvel's "Ant-Man
and the Wasp: Quantumania,"

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.534
which is in theaters now.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.200
He also stars in "Creed III,"

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.934
which opens in theaters
and IMAX March 3rd.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.167
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.868
-I was the best, though.

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:18.734
-Yeah, you were.

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.000
-I was, bro.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.567
But I never got a chance
to prove that.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.767
Look, all I'm saying, bro...

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:32.133
if Apollo Creed could take
a chance on some underdog...

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.868
...why can't you?

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.567
-Please welcome back to the show
Jonathan Majors, everybody!

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:49.434
♪♪

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:57.300
♪♪

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:05.200
♪♪

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.334
I mean, I --

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.634
I don't usually
go out of my way to say this.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:13.033
I am digging your outfit
a great deal.

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.467
-Whoa!
-Yeah.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:15.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you!

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.868
It feels like --

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:20.100
I feel like this is, like,
a '70s talk show right now.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.133
-Yeah, yeah.
-Good old-school vibe.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.167
-We've got our tea.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.234
-We've got our tea.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:26.534
-And now, I know you --

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:29.701
This is rare for a guest to
bring out their own cup.

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.267
But this is -- I've heard you
talk about this,

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.767
this is inspired by something
your mother told you?

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:35.033
-Yes, don't let nobody else
fill you up, boy.

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:36.667
-Uh-huh.
-That works many ways,

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:37.734
doesn't it?

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.801
But she was talking about
self-esteem and respect

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:43.434
and, you know,
what this world can do to you.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.067
You know,
someone can big you up,

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.434
and people can tear you down.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:48.767
But the cup is a metaphor
of, you know,

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.000
you can only do that yourself.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.133
-You can only
fill up your own cup.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.634
It's a good thing
for all of us to remember.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.167
-Another thing to remember

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.434
is to not chew gum
on public television.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:01.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:04.300
-Wait, here.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.634
There you go. You can --
I would --

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:06.801
-You sure?
-Yeah, it's my cup.

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.667
you can go for it. Do it.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:11.067
There you go.

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:12.534
We take care of our guests here.

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.834
-We're officially brothers now.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:17.934
-Yeah, we're officially
brothers.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.734
We're cup brothers.
-Cup brothers.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.367
[ Laughter ]
This is getting weird.

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:22.701
-Doesn't sound right.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.367
I thought it before I said it,

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:25.734
and I didn't realize
how it would sound.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.901
-Perhaps we play
on the same baseball team.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.801
-Yeah, that's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:34.067
We played on the same baseball
team that was short on gear.

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:37.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:39.934
And you -- you would bat first,

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.367
and then depending whether
or not you were on base,

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.467
we'd go to the back --
not important, yeah.

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:46.200
Hey, so last time we talked,
it was on Zoom.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.167
You were in London working
on "Ant-Man," now it's out.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.901
-Now it's out.
-It must be so nice when you,

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:51.567
especially when you work on
one of those Marvel movies

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:53.267
where people know what
you're doing,

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:54.801
can't tell them
any of the details.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:55.868
-Right.
-Is it rewarding

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:57.434
that people
can now experience it?

00:02:57.434 --> 00:03:00.734
-There was a Kang, it was in the
bag, now it's out of the bag.

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.200
-It's out of the bag.
-The Kang is out of the bag.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.701
-Kang's out of the bag.
-Yeah, so --

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.701
Yeah, it feels really good.

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:09.901
You know what I mean?
It's a diary.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:12.267
It's seven months of your life
and prep.

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:13.534
And people saying,
"What you doing?"

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:14.567
Saying, "Oh, nothing, bro."

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:15.968
[ Laughter ]
You know?

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.267
"What you doing in London?"

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:18.868
"Hmm, hanging out," you know?

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:21.267
But, yeah, now it's out,
in the world, it's in cinemas,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.634
it's doing great
at the box office.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.200
-That's very exciting.
-I'm happy, yeah.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.634
-And now, you're actually
in a film that has a chance

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:29.701
to maybe knock your other movie
out of the number-one slot.

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.434
And this is, you know --
this is,

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.334
you know,
the "Rocky" cinematic universe.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:36.501
And these movies, I think
there's a lot of responsibility

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.267
to be in them because
they are so inspirational.

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:39.234
-Yeah.
-And have been

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:40.534
from the very first one.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:42.000
-Were you someone that,
when you saw him as a kid,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.234
you were inspired
by those movies?

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:44.534
-Extremely.
-Yeah.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:46.501
-"Rocky I"
is just a piece of art.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:47.968
-It really is.
It's a perfect movie.

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:49.334
-It's just incredible.
And the story, you know,

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:50.734
Sly and how he got it made.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:52.901
Now in adulthood I go,
"Wow, that's incredible."

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:57.000
The "Creed" films,
"Creed I," I think --

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.667
I was living in New York City?

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:00.267
Yeah. Between schools.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.267
And I joined Equinox...

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.367
[ Light laughter ]
Yeah.

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:05.934
...but was not working.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:07.434
Was not -- Was not an actor.

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:09.501
You know, I was trying to
get to grad school.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.467
So, I could not afford Equinox.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:13.067
-So, that's okay.

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:15.934
And then "Creed II"
was extremely inspiring.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:17.501
Brought a bunch of guys
over to watch it.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.367
You know, I was in grad school
at the time.

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:23.701
Yeah, but that was --
those, um...

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:26.033
the montages, that's the --
that's the kicker.

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:28.467
-Yeah. Those montages --
and I think there's --

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.067
any thing you're about to
take on in your life,

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:31.868
you go back and watch
any "Rocky" montage,

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.567
you're more prepared.
-You're ready. You're ready.

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.868
You're ready. That was really
the pressure for the film.

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:37.601
-And Michael B. Jordan,
true story,

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:39.634
called you personally
to ask you to do this, yes?

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:41.334
-Hit me on the iPhone.
-Yeah?

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:42.400
-Yeah.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:45.801
-And did you answer right away?

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.234
Did you have his number?
Did you know who it was?

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.467
-I did not have
his number right away.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:51.968
He hit my manager and friend,
she said, "Hey,

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:53.501
Michael B. Jordan
wants your phone number."

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:55.000
I said, "Oh, no."

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.734
-Are you someone
who usually gets in trouble?

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.567
-Always. That's exactly it!
You nailed it!

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:00.868
Always in trouble.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.334
'Cause I was like,
if anybody wants to call me,

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:03.934
I've done something.
-Right.

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:05.667
-So, I'm thinking,
"Okay, who did I --

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.667
No, I'm okay, I'm okay."
-Yeah.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.501
-But, yeah, he called me.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:12.901
20 -- 20 minutes into it
I'm nodding my head, you know.

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:14.567
It's a boxing match.
The pitch.

00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:15.701
You know, he's saying things.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:19.467
I'm going, "Hm, hm, hm,
that sounds good.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.901
Ow, take that," you know?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:25.067
-And at the end of it, after
maybe 45 minutes, we hung up.

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:26.901
20 minutes later,
I called him back.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.501
I said, "Hey, man,
let's roll, let's do it."

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:29.801
-That's fantastic.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.834
And now, of course,
this is the kind of role,

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:33.534
and again,
you've been in series movies

00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:36.734
where, you know, there's a
physical fitness element to it.

00:05:36.734 --> 00:05:38.767
I've read how seriously
you took it.

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:40.868
But there has to be --
I mean, I've seen pictures.

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:42.400
The only way
you can take it is seriously

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.767
if the goal is to look like that
at the end.

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:46.033
-Yeah, you must.
-Yeah.

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:47.501
-You must. I mean --

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:48.834
-You can't show up
on the first day and be like,

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.601
"You guys have CGI, right?
You're gonna...?"

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:52.701
[ Laughter ]
-That's the other franchise.

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:53.934
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.
-That's the other franchise.

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:55.100
Yeah, yeah. This is a --

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.667
I mean, that's like --
that's, like, the thing.

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:58.634
You never know --
I mean, you're an entertainer.

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:01.100
You never know what it is that's
going to come across your desk.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.467
-Yeah, I know
it's not going to be

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:03.701
"Do you want to be
in our boxing movie?"

00:06:03.701 --> 00:06:05.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:07.434
-But it might be the --
-Well, Michael B. Jordan

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:09.067
called me,
and I was like, "What?"

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:10.901
And he goes, "Do you have
Jonathan Majors' phone number?"

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:11.901
And I was like --

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:15.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.467
But, yeah, you never know.
-Yeah, you never know.

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:20.467
And I mean -- Sly Stallone,

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:23.000
Sylvester Stallone, you know,
Michael B. Jordan, you know,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.100
all the folks that have
done these films,

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.300
that montage is everything.
-Yeah.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.567
-You know, it's everything.
So yeah, you got tip-top shape.

00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:32.300
I was like a year --
a year and a half,

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.067
year and a half of training,
you know.

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:35.534
-Wow.
-Up until that day.

00:06:35.534 --> 00:06:37.601
-Did you -- After that day,
did you have --

00:06:37.601 --> 00:06:39.200
did you give yourself
a cheat day?

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.400
Was there any enjoyment?
-No, I -- Yes, it was --

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.801
I mean, getting up those ropes
was a lot of fun.

00:06:44.801 --> 00:06:45.801
-Right.
-Especially once you

00:06:45.801 --> 00:06:47.534
got up there.
-Yeah.

00:06:47.534 --> 00:06:49.300
-But, no, right after that,
I shot this other film

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.467
called "Magazine Dreams."

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:52.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.033 --> 00:06:53.267
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:55.033
And that's a --
that's a body builder,

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:56.534
and that's
whole different level of --

00:06:56.534 --> 00:06:57.968
-When are you going to play
somebody who's just, like,

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:58.968
letting himself go?

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:00.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:01.968
-I don't know.

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:04.467
[ Laughter ]
-Give it a few years.

00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:05.667
Yeah, later in your career,
maybe later.

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:07.367
-Yes, soon. Soon I hope, yeah.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:07.367 --> 00:07:08.801
-I got a lot more questions
for you.

00:07:08.801 --> 00:07:10.968
We'll be right back with more
from Jonathan Majors, everybody!

